From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:13:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: ack a remote that restarts without toggling
 restart_done

qcom_smp2p_check_ssr() reset the last value of every inbound entry on
each interrupt, not only when a restart was detected as intended, so
every interrupt replayed every set bit as a new rising edge (the WCSS
remoteproc's "Handover signaled, but it already happened").

A version 1 remote with the SSR ack feature can also restart without
toggling restart_done: the IPQ5018 WCSS firmware clears its entries and
waits for the restart ack, which the host never sent, so its restart
after a crash timed out. Treat entries that all went from set to clear
as such a restart too, and ack it. Measured with the root PD crashing:
the firmware rings with every entry clear 80 ms after its reset, and
reports ready 3 ms after the ack.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
index af0ceeaf6..1242cd142 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -186,6 +186,8 @@ static bool qcom_smp2p_check_ssr(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p)
 {
 	struct smp2p_smem_item *in = smp2p->in;
 	struct smp2p_entry *entry;
+	bool was_set = false;
+	bool cleared = true;
 	bool restart_done;
 	bool restart;
 
@@ -194,10 +196,26 @@ static bool qcom_smp2p_check_ssr(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p)
 
 	restart_done = in->flags & BIT(SMP2P_FLAGS_RESTART_DONE_BIT);
 	restart = restart_done != smp2p->ssr_ack;
-	list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node) {
-		if (!entry->value)
-			continue;
-		entry->last_value = 0;
+
+	/*
+	 * A version 1 remote can also restart without toggling restart_done
+	 * (the IPQ5018 WCSS does): it clears its entries and waits for the ack.
+	 */
+	if (!restart && in->version == 1) {
+		list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node) {
+			if (!entry->value)
+				continue;
+			if (entry->last_value)
+				was_set = true;
+			if (readl(entry->value))
+				cleared = false;
+		}
+		restart = was_set && cleared;
+	}
+
+	if (restart) {
+		list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node)
+			entry->last_value = 0;
 	}
 
 	return restart;
